      ":question/problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{2}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{2},$ we get $x=2,$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{2}={2}^{1/3}\n$$",
